==German==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|de|gmh|gegen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|gagan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*gagin}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|tegen}}, {{cog|en|against}}, {{cog|is|gegn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈɡe.ɡən/|[ˈɡeː.ɡn̩]|[ˈɡeː.ɡŋ̍]}}
* {{audio|de|De-gegen.ogg|audio}}

===Preposition===
{{head|de|preposition}} {{tlb|de|+ accusative}}

# [[against]]
#: {{ux|de|Die Erklärung der Vereinten Nationen über die Beseitigung der Gewalt '''gegen''' Frauen.|The United Nations Declaration on the Elimination of Violence '''against''' Women.}}

====Usage notes====
* Like its Middle High German predecessor, ''gegen'' was formerly also used with the dative, especially by [[Upper German]] writers. Compare {{m|de|entgegen}}, which still takes dative.

